{
  "reviews": [
    {
      "id": "R1",
      "criteria": {
        "credible_improvement_required": {
          "verdict": "pass",
          "score": 4,
          "rationale": "The supplied startup excerpt says \"Using 'MARLIN' Mxfp4 MoE backend.\" The installed Humming selector exposes an override, establishing a concrete activation lead. MARLIN versus Humming, followed by grouped versus indexed at fixed precision, separates the two mechanisms. Exposed expert cost and H200 gains remain unknown; measuring them is a legitimate first falsification step."
        },
        "h200_applicability_and_correctness_required": {
          "verdict": "unknown",
          "score": 3,
          "rationale": "The #59488 patch supplies an SM90 selector restricted to compatible communication, but pinned-loader registration and effective EP4 transport remain unknown. The supplied port-check artifact also reports that #59488 does not apply completely. Routing, rounding, empty ranks, graph replay, target/drafter behavior and quality checks are appropriately proposed; they do not establish current eligibility."
        },
        "discriminating_experiment": {
          "verdict": "pass",
          "score": 4,
          "rationale": "The three fixed arms, eligible-call denominators, complete expert-boundary timing, all-rank speculation counters, held-out traffic and alternating full-run confirmation distinguish backend effects from GEMM selection. Useful-improvement thresholds and guardrail margins still need concrete definitions."
        },
        "traceable_engineering_support": {
          "verdict": "pass",
          "score": 4,
          "rationale": "Observed supplied artifacts establish MARLIN startup selection and the existing override. The source change establishes the proposed automatic-selection predicate. The statement \"the indexed GEMM is much faster for this model\" is a #59488 author claim without a supplied effect size. The draft correctly treats improvement over this deployment as transfer inference."
        },
        "practical_value_and_portfolio_coverage": {
          "verdict": "pass",
          "score": 4,
          "rationale": "Existing controls offer inexpensive falsification and rollback before a source port. This also establishes the incumbent needed by the precision and fusion experiments. Integration cost becomes unknown if explicit Humming selection cannot reach the installed loader; parameterized full-node cost is appropriate."
        }
      },
      "factual_support": "pass",
      "objections": [
        "The startup excerpt covers one identified worker; it does not establish executed backend/schema coverage across both replicas, every rank and both models.",
        "The failed #59488 patch-application check should be included explicitly in the integration assessment.",
        "SGLang #40417 reports that changing a shape-estimation heuristic regressed serving despite favorable kernel comparisons. Its environment identifies L20X, so this is a caution about tuning and graph effects, not direct target-H200 evidence."
      ],
      "required_revision": "Deferred at 76/100 because applicability is unknown. Make the first deliverable an explicit-loader and communication eligibility table for the pinned build. Retain the existing backend/GEMM controls, document the failed patch application, and record selected tuning variants and hint values alongside actual routed rows."
    },
    {
      "id": "R2",
      "criteria": {
        "credible_improvement_required": {
          "verdict": "pass",
          "score": 4,
          "rationale": "Reducing activation traffic and changing expert arithmetic is a credible mechanism, with quantization overhead as a competing cost. Fixed-Humming BF16 versus verified per-token FP8 isolates the precision delta, while retaining MARLIN and the best static backend prevents a misleading local win. The explicit schema inspection addresses unresolved baseline support."
        },
        "h200_applicability_and_correctness_required": {
          "verdict": "unknown",
          "score": 3,
          "rationale": "Per-token FP8 has relevant H200 engineering evidence, and excluding block-FP8/MXFP8 addresses the supplied 0.1.16 restrictions. However, installed named-format plumbing, actual W1/W2 schemas and target/drafter inheritance remain unknown. Proposed scale, clipping, graph and quality checks are suitable but not completed evidence."
        },
        "discriminating_experiment": {
          "verdict": "pass",
          "score": 4,
          "rationale": "Fallback-disabled schema verification, separate W1/W2 opportunities, complete quantization-plus-expert timing, fixed GEMM selection and dependency-matched arms support attribution. Acceptance is correctly diagnostic. The quality subset, noninferiority margin, useful gain and maximum experiment budget remain unspecified."
        },
        "traceable_engineering_support": {
          "verdict": "pass",
          "score": 4,
          "rationale": "#60600 provides schema checks and a reproducible failure report: \"the input silently becomes per-token FP8 instead.\" Its author reports 72.2 us for per-token FP8 versus 110.9 us for BF16 at M4096/N2048/K4096 on H200; routed-MoE behavior and quantization-cost inclusion are not established by that passage. #61875 states \"DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash was not run\" and cannot supply target quality or gain evidence."
        },
        "practical_value_and_portfolio_coverage": {
          "verdict": "pass",
          "score": 4,
          "rationale": "This is a useful precision experiment after Humming eligibility is established. Small-batch latency, quality and acceptance tradeoffs are recognized. Its dependency on the backend experiment should prevent duplicate setup and premature implementation."
        }
      },
      "factual_support": "pass",
      "objections": [
        "The H200 dense probe supports testing per-token FP8, not predicting full-size EP4 MoE or serving improvement.",
        "The named activation option may require a port on the pinned branch; the existing Humming input-schema environment control deserves an explicit eligibility check first.",
        "A generic quality subset does not yet define how native agent behavior, truncation and long reasoning/tool-use failures will be scored."
      ],
      "required_revision": "Deferred at 76/100 because applicability is unknown. Specify the cheapest verified configuration route before proposing a named-format port. Publish requested versus resolved W1/W2 schemas for target and drafter, and define numerical tolerances, quality margins and complete-boundary timing before future execution."
    },
    {
      "id": "R3",
      "criteria": {
        "credible_improvement_required": {
          "verdict": "pass",
          "score": 4,
          "rationale": "The installed selector and supplied patch establish a concrete configuration delta. Fewer projection tiles can reduce repeated post-mapping work. The unchanged synchronous configuration is the appropriate simple comparator, and counting actual small-token calls can cheaply determine whether the mechanism matters to primary traffic."
        },
        "h200_applicability_and_correctness_required": {
          "verdict": "unknown",
          "score": 4,
          "rationale": "The patch explicitly guards SM90 and returns \"return 12, hidden_size // 512, 256\"; H5120 satisfies that condition. The source-hunk application check succeeds. However, live hc_mult and the delayed-kernel call path are not established. Numerical, warmup, replay and fallback checks are well scoped; the application check excludes tests and native dependencies."
        },
        "discriminating_experiment": {
          "verdict": "pass",
          "score": 4,
          "rationale": "The changed-band denominator, eligible/all-call exposure, unchanged 9–32-token control, boundary tests and separate operator/serving measurements are discriminating. Real DSpark verification and paired full-run confirmation address the source experiment's limitations. Useful-effect thresholds and precise primary operating points remain to be fixed."
        },
        "traceable_engineering_support": {
          "verdict": "pass",
          "score": 5,
          "rationale": "Supplied installed code, implementation patch and application-check artifact directly support the delta. The author reports 9.1–14.1% lower H5120 operator latency on H20 and about 1% lower C1 TPOT under TP8 with synthetic acceptance. The source explicitly says of H100/H200, \"These GPUs are not measured.\" The draft correctly retains the unrelated H7168/M128 failure and avoids transferring those gains."
        },
        "practical_value_and_portfolio_coverage": {
          "verdict": "pass",
          "score": 4,
          "rationale": "This is a bounded selector/warmup port with straightforward rollback. Value may be confined to low-load or ragged small-token launches, and the proposal explicitly permits a diagnostic-only outcome. It provides a stronger synchronous comparator for the overlap proposal."
        }
      },
      "factual_support": "pass",
      "objections": [
        "Seq64 and k5 do not establish that primary traffic executes the changed band; the proposal appropriately treats this as an exposure question.",
        "The patch condition uses num_tokens <= 8 without a positive lower bound. Zero-token bypass must be established at the caller or explicitly tested.",
        "Successful source-hunk application is not a complete port, warmup-test or numerical-validation result."
      ],
      "required_revision": "Deferred at 82/100 because target dispatch eligibility remains unknown. Establish the delayed caller and hc_mult, document zero-token handling, and retain the application-check scope. Keep any TF32 repair identical in both arms and report primary-workload exposure separately from low-load diagnostic value."
    },
    {
      "id": "R4",
      "criteria": {
        "credible_improvement_required": {
          "verdict": "pass",
          "score": 3,
          "rationale": "Hiding dependency-independent coefficient work is a credible testable mechanism, and the installed SM100-only gate establishes a source delta. Checking the TP1 dependency window before implementation is appropriate. The proposal correctly avoids claiming a TP all-reduce saving; the available independent work remains unknown."
        },
        "h200_applicability_and_correctness_required": {
          "verdict": "unknown",
          "score": 3,
          "rationale": "An explicit guarded SM90 port is described, with a credible separate TF32 repair path. However, the complete overlap schedule, executed JIT artifact and Hopper stream/graph correctness are unverified. #60768 states \"These mock capability checks validate dispatch only.\" The compensated-BF16 failure does not veto this distinct TF32 proposal."
        },
        "discriminating_experiment": {
          "verdict": "pass",
          "score": 4,
          "rationale": "Useful concurrent execution is distinguished from auxiliary-stream activity, and the complete critical path is compared against the strongest synchronous configuration. Corrected artifacts in both arms, fallback tests, eligible denominators and paired confirmation are appropriate. The exact independent operation and allowable stream-ordering window still need specification."
        },
        "traceable_engineering_support": {
          "verdict": "pass",
          "score": 4,
          "rationale": "The supplied gate and TF32 header support the baseline concerns. #448 shows the register-lifetime repair, while #59129 says \"There is no throughput improvement claim for this correctness repair.\" SGLang's H200 TP8/EP1 results are a multi-change bundle without an overlap ablation. Isolated overlap hardware results, workload effects and effect size remain unknown."
        },
        "practical_value_and_portfolio_coverage": {
          "verdict": "pass",
          "score": 3,
          "rationale": "A source-only dependency check limits initial cost, but integration and stream correctness are substantially harder than launch tuning. Both mHC proposals may depend on the same small-token traffic. This remains a conditional research lead with uncertain primary-workload value."
        }
      },
      "factual_support": "pass",
      "objections": [
        "No supplied dependency graph identifies which operation can overlap coefficient computation at TP1.",
        "The installed header ordering does not prove that the running cached binary executes the affected code or has produced incorrect outputs.",
        "SGLang's bundled gain and the separate compensated-BF16 failure establish neither success nor failure of this overlap-only port."
      ],
      "required_revision": "Deferred at 67/100, below threshold and with applicability unknown. Name the TP1-independent operation, its producers/consumers and required stream events before a build. Identify the executed TF32 artifact and compare against the best synchronous configuration using the same verified arithmetic and repair."
    },
    {
      "id": "R5",
      "criteria": {
        "credible_improvement_required": {
          "verdict": "pass",
          "score": 4,
          "rationale": "Fusing dispatch, expert computation and combine can remove staging and launch overhead relative to the supplied separate expert path. The proposed eligibility review is concrete and precedes implementation. Comparing against the best validated static backend is appropriate; exposed communication cost and target gains remain unknown."
        },
        "h200_applicability_and_correctness_required": {
          "verdict": "unknown",
          "score": 2,
          "rationale": "Exact FlashInfer FP4 API availability, plan legality, scale conversion and swiglu_limit10 behavior are unresolved on 0.7.0.post1. Supplied DeepGEMM #411/#473 patches provide additional SM90 paths whose visible dimensional checks admit the target geometry, but the excerpts do not establish clamp semantics or complete eligibility. These are gaps, not demonstrated incompatibility."
        },
        "discriminating_experiment": {
          "verdict": "pass",
          "score": 3,
          "rationale": "The plan covers fused-call opportunities, per-group capacity agreement, valid/processed tokens, memory/KV loss, idle ranks, skew and held-out capacity boundaries. Dependency-matched controls are valuable. However, matching native weights alone does not isolate fusion if activation quantization, scale granularity or rounding also changes."
        },
        "traceable_engineering_support": {
          "verdict": "pass",
          "score": 3,
          "rationale": "#6517 supplies a concrete cleanup failure and author-reported tests, but its implementation patch is unavailable. Its H200 push claim explicitly leaves \"H20 and EP4 plans unchanged.\" #62603 concerns block-FP8 weights and GLM serving, including low-load TTFT and oversized-workspace regressions. These reports motivate the adapter; they do not establish native-MXFP4 V4.1 behavior."
        },
        "practical_value_and_portfolio_coverage": {
          "verdict": "pass",
          "score": 3,
          "rationale": "Fusion adds communication and staging coverage beyond expert GEMM tuning, but has the highest and currently unknown integration cost. Eligibility-first stopping and fixed initial plans contain scope. Workspace duplication, KV loss and low-load tails could erase value, so this is a conditional port investigation rather than a ready serving experiment."
        }
      },
      "factual_support": "pass",
      "objections": [
        "Scope the SM100 restriction to the integrated vLLM backend described by #62603. Supplied DeepGEMM #411/#473 contain SM90 implementation paths and deserve an explicit eligibility comparison.",
        "E384/EP4 divisibility and passing visible dimension checks do not establish clamped SwiGLU, scale representability, complete planner legality or graph safety.",
        "A faster fused arm could reflect changed activation arithmetic or weight-scale conversion. The current experiment does not fully isolate those effects from fusion."
      ],
      "required_revision": "Deferred at 63/100, below threshold and with applicability unknown. Build a branch/API eligibility matrix for FlashInfer and the supplied SM90 DeepGEMM paths. Require clamp-active and scale-boundary reference cases. Define a numerically matched unfused comparator where available; otherwise report a combined backend/precision effect and keep fusion attribution unresolved."
    }
  ],
  "global_gaps": [
    "All five have credible testable mechanisms, but each retains an unknown required applicability gate. Weighted scores do not override that gate. Deferral does not reject cheap eligibility checks or later bounded experiments, and no measured H200 speedup is required to propose them.",
    "Observed evidence here consists of supplied source, configuration, log and application-check artifacts. Performance and validation results from PRs remain author reports. All improvements on the pinned target deployment are transfer hypotheses; no new execution or independent measurement occurred.",
    "Before future execution, specify the primary metric and operating points, minimum useful improvement, numerical/quality margins, tail and memory guardrails, run duration and finite stopping budget. Preserve the existing full-run pairing, drift checks and exclusion of profiled measurements from the serving frontier.",
    "All-replica/rank dispatch and effective communication remain unverified. Bind counter resets, missing coverage, request-to-final-rank joins and clean profiling markers to the common evaluator contract. The supplied packet does not define G01–G05 sufficiently to certify an exact test mapping.",
    "The portfolio contains three related MoE experiments and two small-token mHC experiments. Their dependencies are sensible, but shared activation failures or absent small-token exposure could eliminate several simultaneously; stage eligibility checks before allocating implementation effort.",
    "H200 node price, production SLO and candidate-specific target effects remain unknown. Keep full eight-GPU cost parameterized and goodput conditional on an explicitly declared SLO.",
    "The packet supplies 64 of 204 source records and lists 16 repositories despite referring to 13. Omitted records, title-only leads and full-text-availability metadata do not establish implementation support, comprehensive coverage or absence of counterevidence. Historical novelty decisions are not selection vetoes."
  ]
}
